  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Americas population movement crises  along the migratory routes in South and Central America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Honduras, Panama, Mexico, Costa Rica and Colombia with the respective NSs.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The partnership with the Netherlands Red Cross will seek to improve the response mechanisms of RC systems along the region through the strengthening of the capacities of the National Societies and IFRC Delegation for promoting an effective response. Mostly extending and enhancing the Humanitarian Services Point model through the implementation of preparedness and readiness actions as well as conducting minimum standards to promote harmonization and quality assurance. All the actions will take advantage of the evidence-based humanitarian diplomacy efforts and utilize digital transformation to strengthen the regional capacities for data collection and analysis.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	Implementation of the HSP evaluation tool to determine the status of each point, in accordance with the minimum standard criteria (see the check-list in Annex). 
&#x2022;	Based on the HSP evaluation tool results, harmonize and improve the quality of care in HSPs using the performance checklist or minimum standards.
&#x2022;	To scale-up use of the Red Data initiative in HSPs to ensure connectivity, support RCF services, provide relevant information, and establish an efficient feedback mechanism (further information in Annex).
&#x2022;	To establish cross-border coordination mechanisms to attend to migrants&#x2019; needs.
&#x2022;	Support NSs in training and equipping for migrant care, with emphasis on WASH, MHPPS, PGI, PSEA, Community Engagement and Accountability Mechanisms   and safe referrals.</narrative>
  </description>
